      "section": "Intro",
      "start": 4,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/intro-2.png",
      "background": "livingroom",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Would you fight?",
      "narration": "Alright. Quick question first. Say you have forty-seven thousand men. The enemy has at least twice that, on a flat field they picked and prepared themselves. Do you fight?",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-3",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "Intro",
      "start": 17,
      "duration": 6,
      "image": "images/intro-3.png",
      "background": "livingroom",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "On their field? With half the army? No way. I'd go home.",
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "id": "intro-4",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "Intro",
      "start": 23,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/intro-4.png",
      "background": "livingroom",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "sit"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Most generals would. Alexander was twenty-five. He fought, and he won so completely that the biggest empire on Earth fell apart. Let me show you how.",
      "word_count": 26
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-01",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 35,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-01.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Gaugamela, 1 October 331 BC",
      "narration": "October 1st, 331 BC. A dusty plain in northern Mesopotamia, in what is now Iraq. Two armies face each other in the morning sun, and the fate of the largest empire on Earth is about to be decided in a single day.",
      "word_count": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-02",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 53,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-02.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "On one side, the Persian Empire, the superpower of the ancient world. Its king, Darius the Third, has gathered soldiers from three continents: armored horsemen, elite guards, war elephants, and chariots with blades fixed to their wheels.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-03",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Hook",
      "start": 69,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-03.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Alexander, age 25",
      "narration": "On the other side, a young king from Macedonia, a small kingdom north of Greece, with about forty-seven thousand men. Outnumbered, far from home, with no road back. His name is Alexander.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-04",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Gaugamela",
      "start": 83,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-04.png",
      "background": "mapalex",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "334–331 BC",
      "narration": "Three years earlier, Alexander had crossed into Asia. He beat a Persian army at the Granicus River, then beat Darius himself at Issus, where the Persian king fled the field. Then Alexander swung south and took Egypt without a fight.",
      "word_count": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-05",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Gaugamela",
      "start": 100,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-05.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Immortal",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Darius",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Immortal",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Darius III",
      "narration": "Darius offered peace: a fortune in silver, his daughter's hand in marriage, and every land west of the Euphrates River. Alexander said no. He didn't want half of Persia. He wanted all of it.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-06",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The road to Gaugamela",
      "start": 115,
      "duration": 7,
      "image": "images/shot-06.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Immortal",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Darius",
          "expression": "angry",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "So Darius prepared for one last, decisive battle. And this time, he would choose the ground.",
      "word_count": 16
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-07",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Darius sets a trap",
      "start": 122,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-07.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "A field leveled for chariots",
      "narration": "He picked the wide, open plain of Gaugamela. Then he ordered his men to flatten it, cutting down bushes, leveling bumps and clearing stones, so his chariots could charge at full speed.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-08",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Darius sets a trap",
      "start": 136,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-08.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "These were scythed chariots: horse-drawn carts with long curved blades sticking out from the wheels. Darius had about two hundred of them, and a field as smooth as a racetrack.",
      "word_count": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-09",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Darius sets a trap",
      "start": 149,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-09.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Surround them",
      "narration": "His line stretched for miles, far longer than Alexander's. The plan was simple: wrap around both ends of the Macedonian army and crush it from every side.",
      "word_count": 27
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-10",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Darius sets a trap",
      "start": 161,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-10.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "How many Persians?",
      "narration": "How many men did Darius have? Ancient writers claimed up to a million, which is almost certainly an exaggeration. Modern historians usually guess around a hundred thousand. Either way, the Macedonians were badly outnumbered.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-11",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Darius sets a trap",
      "start": 176,
      "duration": 12,
      "image": "images/shot-11.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "He even brought fifteen war elephants from India. Any general in the world would have looked at that wall of men and lost his nerve. Almost any general.",
      "word_count": 28
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-12",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 188,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-12.png",
      "background": "plainnight",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "20 September 331 BC",
      "narration": "Eleven nights before the battle, the moon turned a dark red in a lunar eclipse. Both armies saw it as an omen.",
      "word_count": 22
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-13",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 198,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-13.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "And we know the exact dates, because astronomers in Babylon recorded the eclipse on a clay tablet that still survives today. The same tablet mentions the battle itself, and the king whose troops deserted him.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-14",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 214,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-14.png",
      "background": "plainnight",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Soldier",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "30 September, night",
      "narration": "On the night of September 30th, the two armies camped just a few miles apart. The Macedonians could see the Persian campfires glowing across the whole plain, like a city of lights.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-15",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 228,
      "duration": 10,
      "image": "images/shot-15.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Parmenion",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Parmenion",
      "narration": "Parmenion, Alexander's oldest and most experienced general, had an idea: attack now, at night, while the enemy can't see how few we are.",
      "word_count": 23
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-16",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 238,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-16.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Parmenion",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "“I will not steal my victory.”",
      "narration": "Alexander refused. According to the ancient writers, he answered: “I will not steal my victory.” A win in the dark could be blamed on luck. He wanted to beat Darius in broad daylight, so no one could ever say the Persians weren't truly beaten.",
      "word_count": 44
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-night-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 257,
      "duration": 7,
      "image": "images/talk-night-1.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Okay, that sounds cool, but isn't it a dumb risk? A night attack sounds smart.",
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-night-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 264,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/talk-night-2.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Honestly? Parmenion's plan had a real chance. But night attacks back then were chaos: men got lost, units ran into each other. And Alexander had a bigger goal. If Darius lost a fair fight, nobody in Persia could argue he still deserved to be king.",
      "word_count": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-17",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 283,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-17.png",
      "background": "plainnight",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Persian",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Persian",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Immortal",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Darius, meanwhile, was afraid of exactly that night attack. So he kept his whole army standing in formation, in their armor, all night long. By sunrise, they were exhausted.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-18",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The night before",
      "start": 296,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-18.png",
      "background": "tent",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "sit"
        },
        {
          "name": "Parmenion",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "And Alexander? He slept so deeply that his generals had to wake him in the morning. When they asked how he could sleep at a time like this, he reportedly said the hard part was over: Darius had finally agreed to fight.",
      "word_count": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-19",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Battle lines",
      "start": 314,
      "duration": 19,
      "image": "images/shot-19.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Dawn, 1 October",
      "narration": "At dawn, Alexander set up his army. In the center stood the phalanx. On the right, Alexander himself with his elite Companion Cavalry. On the left, his general Parmenion. And behind them, a second line, ready to turn around if the Persians got behind them.",
      "word_count": 45
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-20",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Battle lines",
      "start": 333,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-20.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The phalanx",
      "narration": "The phalanx was the backbone of the army. Each man carried a sarissa, a pike almost six meters long. With several rows of points sticking out in front, it was a moving hedge of iron that nobody wanted to walk into.",
      "word_count": 41
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-21",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Battle lines",
      "start": 351,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-21.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Alexander moves right",
      "narration": "Then Alexander did something strange. Instead of charging forward, he led his right wing sideways, to the right, at an angle. Step by step, he was pulling the battle off the smooth ground Darius had prepared.",
      "word_count": 36
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-22",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "Battle lines",
      "start": 367,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-22.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Darius saw the danger. If the Macedonians got off his leveled field, his chariots would be useless. So he sent horsemen from his left wing racing out to block Alexander and get around him.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-23",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The chariot charge",
      "start": 382,
      "duration": 7,
      "image": "images/shot-23.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The chariot charge",
      "narration": "Then Darius played his big card. The scythed chariots charged straight at the Macedonian line.",
      "word_count": 15
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-24",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The chariot charge",
      "start": 389,
      "duration": 20,
      "image": "images/shot-24.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Open the lanes!",
      "narration": "But Alexander was ready. Light troops in front aimed at the drivers and grabbed the horses' reins. And when the chariots reached the phalanx, the soldiers simply stepped aside, opening lanes. The chariots raced harmlessly through the gaps, where the troops behind them pulled the drivers down.",
      "word_count": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-chariots-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "The chariot charge",
      "start": 409,
      "duration": 4,
      "image": "images/talk-chariots-1.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Wait, they just... moved out of the way?",
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-chariots-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "The chariot charge",
      "start": 413,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/talk-chariots-2.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "That's the whole secret. It sounds easy, but imagine standing still while blades come at you, and stepping aside at exactly the right second, all together. That takes years of drill. Darius had the fancy weapon. Alexander had the discipline.",
      "word_count": 40
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-25",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 430,
      "duration": 18,
      "image": "images/shot-25.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "The gap",
      "narration": "Meanwhile, Darius kept sending more and more horsemen to the left to stop Alexander's sideways march. And every unit he sent stretched his own line thinner. Then it happened: a gap opened in the Persian line, right in front of Darius himself.",
      "word_count": 42
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-26",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 448,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-26.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "This was the moment Alexander had been waiting for. He stopped moving right and gathered his Companion Cavalry into a huge wedge, like an arrowhead, with himself at the tip.",
      "word_count": 30
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-27",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 461,
      "duration": 13,
      "image": "images/shot-27.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "quick push in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Charge!",
      "narration": "Then he turned and charged straight into the gap, aiming at one man: Darius. Right behind him, the phalanx lowered its pikes and pushed forward like a moving wall.",
      "word_count": 29
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-28",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 474,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-28.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The Persian guards in the center tried to close the gap, but it was too late. The wedge was already inside.",
      "word_count": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-gap-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 483,
      "duration": 7,
      "image": "images/talk-gap-1.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "surprised",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "He went straight for the king? The leader charging in front? Isn't that crazy?",
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-gap-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "The gap",
      "start": 490,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/talk-gap-2.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Crazy risky, yes. But also smart. In an army like Persia's, everything depended on the king. Every order came from him. Scare him off the field, and the whole machine stops working.",
      "word_count": 32
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-29",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The king runs",
      "start": 504,
      "duration": 21,
      "image": "images/shot-29.png",
      "background": "paper",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "A famous ancient mosaic from Pompeii shows a moment just like this: Alexander charging bareheaded, and Darius in his chariot, turning away with terror on his face. Historians still argue whether it shows Gaugamela or Issus, but it shows how the ancient world remembered these two men.",
      "word_count": 47
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-30",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The king runs",
      "start": 525,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-30.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan right",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "As the Macedonians fought their way closer, the driver beside Darius was struck down. The King of Kings turned his chariot around and fled the battlefield. For the second time, Darius ran from Alexander.",
      "word_count": 34
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-31",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The king runs",
      "start": 540,
      "duration": 15,
      "image": "images/shot-31.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow pan left",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "The news spread across the plain like an earthquake. The king is gone! Persian soldiers who were still fighting, even winning in some places, lost heart. They began to fall back, and then to run.",
      "word_count": 35
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-32",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The king runs",
      "start": 555,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/shot-32.png",
      "background": "battlemap",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Parmenion in trouble",
      "narration": "Not everything went Alexander's way. On the far left, Parmenion was in serious trouble, surrounded by Persian horsemen, and he sent riders begging for help. So Alexander gave up the chase and turned back to rescue his old general.",
      "word_count": 39
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-33",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "The king runs",
      "start": 572,
      "duration": 9,
      "image": "images/shot-33.png",
      "background": "plain",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "By sunset, it was over. The greatest army of the East had been broken on the very field it had chosen.",
      "word_count": 21
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-34",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 581,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-34.png",
      "background": "babylon",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Citizen",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Citizen",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "Babylon, 331 BC",
      "narration": "Weeks later, Alexander rode into Babylon, one of the richest cities on Earth, and its people came out to welcome him. Soon the royal city of Susa opened its gates too, and within months Persepolis had fallen.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-35",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 597,
      "duration": 14,
      "image": "images/shot-35.png",
      "background": "plainnight",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Darius",
          "expression": "closed",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": "330 BC",
      "narration": "And Darius? He kept running. Within a year he was gone, betrayed and struck down by his own nobles. The empire his family had ruled for more than two hundred years was finished.",
      "word_count": 33
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-36",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 611,
      "duration": 16,
      "image": "images/shot-36.png",
      "background": "mapalex",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": "Alexander's empire",
      "narration": "Alexander kept marching, all the way to India. In about ten years, he built one of the largest empires the world had ever seen, and spread Greek language and culture from Egypt to the edge of India.",
      "word_count": 37
    },
    {
      "id": "shot-37",
      "speaker": null,
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 627,
      "duration": 11,
      "image": "images/shot-37.png",
      "background": "parchment",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "He never lost a major battle. He died young, at just thirty-two. And at Gaugamela, the battle that ended an empire, he was only twenty-five.",
      "word_count": 25
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-lesson-1",
      "speaker": "son",
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 638,
      "duration": 4,
      "image": "images/talk-lesson-1.png",
      "background": "babylon",
      "camera": "static",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "determined",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "So the lesson is that numbers don't matter?",
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "id": "talk-lesson-2",
      "speaker": "father",
      "section": "What came next",
      "start": 642,
      "duration": 17,
      "image": "images/talk-lesson-2.png",
      "background": "babylon",
      "camera": "slow zoom in",
      "characters": [
        {
          "name": "Alexander",
          "expression": "smug",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Father",
          "expression": "gentle",
          "pose": "stand"
        },
        {
          "name": "Son",
          "expression": "neutral",
          "pose": "stand"
        }
      ],
      "on_screen_text": null,
      "narration": "Numbers matter a lot. Most of the time, the bigger army wins. But Gaugamela shows what can beat them: a clever plan, soldiers drilled to perfection, and a leader who spots the one moment that counts, and doesn't hesitate.",
      "word_count": 39
    },
    {
